From 66fb7891b7d7cb4b00c00b6e57cdd1d2c58aa1ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 08:12:36 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] tu/kgsl: implement VK_EXT_external_memory_host

Import host pointers with IOCTL_KGSL_GPUOBJ_IMPORT (KGSL_USER_MEM_TYPE_ADDR).
KGSL pins the pages and maps them into the GPU address space. Imports are
always IO-coherent and write-back cached, so the extension is only exposed
when the kernel supports that memory type, and only cached+coherent memory
types are reported by vkGetMemoryHostPointerPropertiesEXT. The CPU mapping
stays owned by the application: the BO keeps it as its map, is never
unmapped, and kgsl_bo_finish no longer munmaps host-pointer BOs.

Lets emulators on unified-memory Adreno devices let the GPU read and write
guest RAM in place instead of copying it into driver-allocated memory.
Tested on Adreno 830 (KGSL, GKI 6.x) with memfd-backed MAP_SHARED memory:
CPU writes through a second mapping are visible to GPU copies, GPU fills and
copies are visible to the CPU, buffers bound at offsets inside one import
alias correctly, overlapping imports work, and unaligned imports fail.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
